onary black holes in vacuum"]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/767100"}},{"reference":{"label":"33","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"11","artid":"1","year":2010,"page_start":"1","journal_title":"Ann.Inst.H.Poincare Phys.Theor."},"title":{"title":"On Hawking’s local rigidity theorem for charged black holes"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Yu, P."}]},"legacy_curated":true},{"reference":{"label":"34","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"33","artid":"83","year":1973,"page_start":"83","journal_title":"Commun.Math.Phys."},"misc":["Existence, uniqueness, and local stability for the Einstein-Maxwell-Boltzman system"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Bancel, D."},{"full_name":"Choquet-Bruhat, Y."}]},"legacy_curated":true},{"reference":{"label":"35","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"192","artid":"1428","year":2011,"page_start":"1428","journal_title":"Astrophys.J.Suppl."},"misc":["Seven-year Wilkinson microwave anisotropy probe (WMAP) observations: Sky maps, systematic errors, and basic results"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Jarosik, N."},{"full_name":"Bennett, C.L."},{"full_name":"Dunkley, J."},{"full_name":"Gold, B."},{"full_name":"Greason, M.R."},{"full_name":"Halpern, M."},{"full_name":"Hill, R.S."},{"full_name":"Hinshaw, G."},{"full_name":"Kogut, A."},{"full_name":"Komatsu, E."},{"full_name":"Larson, D."},{"full_name":"Limon, M."},{"full_name":"Meyer, S.S."},{"full_name":"Nolta, M.R."},{"full_name":"Odegard, N."},{"full_name":"Page, L."},{"full_name":"Smith, K.M."},{"full_name":"Spergel, D.N."},{"full_name":"Tucker, G.S."},{"full_name":"Weiland, J.L."},{"full_name":"Wollack, E."},{"full_name":"Wright, E.L."}]},"legacy_curated":true},{"reference":{"imprint":{"publisher":"University of Chicago Press,. 111"},"label":"36","publication_info":{"year":1984},"title":{"title":"General Relativity"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Wald, Robert"}]},"legacy_curated":true}],"number_of_pages":120,"referenced_authors_bais":["Stephen.W.Hawking.1","V.A.Belinsky.2","I.M.Khalatnikov.1","R.P.Geroch.1","I.S.Allen.2","J.M.Lee.3","I.Racz.1","Helmut.Friedrich.1","R.M.Wald.1","J.Isenberg.1","A.D.Ionescu.2","R.Penrose.1","S.Klainerman.1","V.Moncrief.1","E.M.Lifshitz.1","Y.Choquet.Bruhat.1","J.Corvino.2","H.Ringstrom.1","P.T.Chrusciel.1"],"legacy_version":"20210206145934.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology"}],"legacy_creation_date":"2015-03-25","author_count":1,"urls":[{"description":"Oregon U. server","value":"http://hdl.handle.net/1794/11543"}],"first_author":{"full_name":"Luo, Xianghui","last_name":"Luo","first_name":"Xianghui","recid":1953641},"control_number":1355471,"earliest_date":"2011-06","document_type":["thesis"],"texkeys":["Luo:2011nda"],"abstracts":[{"value":"This dissertation contains the results obtained from a study of two subjects in mathematical general relativity. The first part of this dissertation is about the existence of Killing symmetries in spacetimes containing a compact Cauchy horizon. We prove the existence of a nontrivial Killing symmetry in a large class of analytic cosmological spacetimes with a compact Cauchy horizon for any spacetime dimension. In doing so, we also remove the restrictive analyticity condition and obtain a generalization to the smooth case. The second part of the dissertation presents our results on the global stability problem for a class of cosmological models. We investigate the power law inflating cosmological models in the presence of electromagnetic fields. A stability result for such cosmological spacetimes is proved. This dissertation includes unpublished co-authored material."}],"persistent_identifiers":[{"schema":"HDL","source":"bibmatch","value":"1794/11543"}],"titles":[{"title":"Symmetries of Cauchy Horizons and Global Stability of Cosmological Models"}],"facet_author_name":["1953641_X. Luo"],"core":true,"thesis_info":{"date":"2011","institutions":[{"curated_relation":true,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903097"},"name":"Oregon U."}],"degree_type":"PhD","defense_date":"2011-06"},"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:1355471","updated":"2024-12-28T02:23:32.520577"},"curated":true,"supervisors":[{"full_name":"Isenberg, James","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1004888"},"last_name":"Isenberg","ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"J.Isenberg.1"}],"inspire_roles":["supervisor"],"signature_block":"ISANBARGj","first_name":"James","uuid":"dff3b225-629c-4c77-80a3-3c64bba7a062","recid":1004888}]},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1355471?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1355471?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1355471?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1355471?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1355471?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1355471?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1355471"},"id":"1355471"},{"created":"2013-05-28T00:00:00+00:00","updated":"2023-03-07T05:19:18.554755+00:00","metadata":{"authors":[{"full_name_unicode_normalized":"moncrief, vincent","full_name":"Moncrief, Vincent","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/997016"},"affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903357"},"value":"Yale U."}],"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"V.Moncrief.1"}],"last_name":"Moncrief","signature_block":"MANCRAFv","first_name":"Vincent","uuid":"4cac3bfb-e0f6-4df9-8be0-c9be464db6e8","recid":997016},{"full_name_unicode_normalized":"isenberg, james","full_name":"Isenberg, James","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1004888"},"affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/909941"},"value":"Oregon U., Dept. Math."}],"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"J.Isenberg.1"}],"last_name":"Isenberg","signature_block":"ISANBARGj","first_name":"James","uuid":"7e107048-437f-49df-9a4a-3e0cea8e613c","recid":1004888}],"citation_count":182,"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"89","page_end":"413","year":1983,"journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214791"},"page_start":"387","journal_issue":"3","journal_title":"Commun.Math.Phys."}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":177,"citeable":true,"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","number_of_pages":27,"legacy_version":"20160405105730.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Math and Math Physics"}],"legacy_creation_date":"2013-05-28","author_count":2,"first_author":{"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/03v76x132"}],"full_name":"Moncrief, Vincent","last_name":"Moncrief","first_name":"Vincent","recid":997016},"control_number":1235595,"dois":[{"value":"10.1007/BF01214662"}],"earliest_date":"1983","document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Moncrief:1983xua"],"abstracts":[{"source":"Springer","value":"We consider analytic vacuum and electrovacuum spacetimes which contain a compact null hypersurface ruled byclosed null generators. We prove that each such spacetime has a non-trivial Killing symmetry. We distinguish two classes of null surfaces, degenerate and non-degenerate ones, characterized by the zero or non-zero value of a constant analogous to the “surface gravity” of stationary black holes. We show that the non-degenerate null surfaces are always Cauchy horizons across which the Killing fields change from spacelike (in the globally hyperbolic regions) to timelike (in the acausal, analytic extensions).","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Springer"}}],"refereed":true,"titles":[{"title":"Symmetries of cosmological Cauchy horizons"}],"facet_author_name":["997016_Vincent Moncrief","1004888_James Isenberg"],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:1235595","updated":"2023-03-07T05:19:18.554755"},"curated":true,"journal_title_variants":["Commun. Math. Phys.","Commun.Math.Phys."]},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1235595?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1235595?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1235595?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1235595?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1235595?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1235595?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1235595"},"id":"1235595"},{"created":"2020-08-28T00:00:00+00:00","updated":"2026-04-01T05:02:03.511540+00:00","metadata":{"authors":[{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Centro de Matemática, Universidad de la República, Montevideo, Uruguay"}],"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"GRID","value":"grid.11630.35"},{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/030bbe882"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"bustamante, ignacio","full_name":"Bustamante, Ignacio","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/2346774"},"last_name":"Bustamante","affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903022"},"value":"Republica U., Montevideo"}],"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"I.Bustamante.1"}],"signature_block":"BASTANANTi","first_name":"Ignacio","uuid":"fb874c32-4e70-465d-bf6d-1f2757f26e5d","recid":2346774},{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Centro de Matemática, Universidad de la República, Montevideo, Uruguay"}],"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"GRID","value":"grid.11630.35"},{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/030bbe882"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"reiris, martín","full_name":"Reiris, Martín","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/2333930"},"last_name":"Reiris","affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903022"},"value":"Republica U., Montevideo"}],"ids":[{"schema":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6368-752X"},{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"M.R.Ithurralde.1"}],"signature_block":"RARm","first_name":"Martín","uuid":"a86c4fc8-4c2d-4897-8381-30ba70976347","recid":2333930}],"citation_count":5,"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"53","artid":"36","year":2021,"journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1214738"},"page_start":"36","journal_issue":"3","journal_title":"Gen.Rel.Grav."}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":5,"citeable":true,"references":[{"reference":{"publication_info":{"year":2015},"label":"1","misc":["MM Alexandrino, RG Bettiol: Lie groups and geometric aspects of isometric actions","Cham"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[1] MM Alexandrino, RG Bettiol: Lie groups and geometric aspects of isometric actions, Springer, Cham, 2015"}]},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1006/aphy.1995.1084"],"label":"2"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[2] PT Chrusciel, AD Rendall: Strong cosmic censorship in vacuum space-times with compact, locally homogeneous Cauchy surfaces, ['Annals Phys.,242,349-385'], DOI: 10.1006/aphy.1995.1084"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/379284"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1088/0264-9381/21/3/010"],"label":"3"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[3] Piotr T Chrusciel: Lake, Kayll: cauchy horizons in gowdy space-times, ['Class.Quant.Grav.,21,S153-S170'], DOI: 10.1088/0264-9381/21/3/010"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/623742"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.4310/jdg/1214442157"],"label":"4"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[4] Kenji Fukaya: A boundary of the set of the Riemannian manifolds with bounded curvatures and diameters, ['J.Diff.Geom.,28,1-21'], DOI: 10.4310/jdg/1214442157"}]},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1088/0264-9381/9/7/004"],"label":"5"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[5] J Isenberg, V Moncrief: On spacetimes containing Killing vector fields with non-closed orbits, ['Class.Quant.Grav.,9,1683'], DOI: 10.1088/0264-9381/9/7/004"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2862904"}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"year":2015},"label":"6","misc":["Larsson, Eric.: Smoothness of compact horizons. In: Annales Henri Poincaré, volume 16, pages 2163-2214","Cham"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[6] Larsson, Eric.: Smoothness of compact horizons. In: Annales Henri Poincaré, volume 16, pages 2163–2214. Springer, Cham (2015)"}]},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"year":2012},"label":"7","misc":[": Introduction to Smooth Manifolds","New York"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Lee, John M."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[7] John M Lee: Introduction to Smooth Manifolds, Springer, New York, 2012"}]},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1063/1.4893877"],"label":"8"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[8] E Minguzzi: Completeness of cauchy horizon generators, ['J.Math.Phys.,55,082503'], DOI: 10.1063/1.4893877"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1302392"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1007/s00220-015-2415-8"],"label":"9"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[9] E Minguzzi: Area theorem and smoothness of compact Cauchy horizons, ['Commun.Math.Phys.,339,57-98'], DOI: 10.1007/s00220-015-2415-8"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1302394"}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"year":1967},"label":"10","misc":[": Taub-Nut Space as a Counterexample to almost anything. Relativity Theory and Astrophysics: Relativity and Cosmology. American Mathematical Society and Cornell University. J","Ehlers Ed., volume 8, page 160"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Misner, C.W."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[10] Misner, C.W.: Taub-Nut Space as a Counterexample to almost anything. Relativity Theory and Astrophysics: Relativity and Cosmology. American Mathematical Society and Cornell University. J. Ehlers Ed., volume 8, page 160 (1967)"}]},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1007/s00220-019-03571-9"],"label":"11"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[11] Vincent Moncrief: Isenberg, James: Symmetries of cosmological Cauchy horizons with non-closed orbits, ['Commun.Math.Phys.,374,145-186'], DOI: 10.1007/s00220-019-03571-9"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1684261"}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"year":1939},"label":"12","misc":["Myers","Steenrod, Norman.Earl.: The group of isometries of a Riemannian manifold. Annals of Mathematics, pages 400-416"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Sumner.B."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[12] Myers, Sumner.B., Steenrod, Norman.Earl.: The group of isometries of a Riemannian manifold. Annals of Mathematics, pages 400–416 (1939)"}]},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1802.10057","publication_info":{"year":2018},"label":"13","misc":["Oliver Lindblad Petersen. Wave equations with initial data on compact Cauchy horizons. arXiv preprint"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[13] Oliver Lindblad Petersen. Wave equations with initial data on compact Cauchy horizons. arXiv preprint arXiv:1802.10057 (2018)"}]},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"1809.02580","publication_info":{"year":2018},"label":"14","misc":["Oliver Lindblad Petersen and István Rácz. Symmetries of vacuum spacetimes with a compact Cauchy horizon of constant non-zero surface gravity"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[14] Oliver Lindblad Petersen and István Rácz. Symmetries of vacuum spacetimes with a compact Cauchy horizon of constant non-zero surface gravity. arXiv:1809.02580 (2018)"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1693202"}},{"reference":{"publication_info":{"year":2020},"label":"15","misc":["Martin Reiris: Bustamante, Ignacio: On the existence of Killing fields in smooth spacetimes with a compact Cauchy horizon., Classical and Quantum Gravity, Accepted manuscript -"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[15] Martin Reiris: Bustamante, Ignacio: On the existence of Killing fields in smooth spacetimes with a compact Cauchy horizon., Classical and Quantum Gravity, Accepted manuscript -, 2020"}]},{"reference":{"arxiv_eprint":"dg-ga/9510002","publication_info":{"year":1995},"label":"16","authors":[{"full_name":"Alan.D."}],"misc":["Rendall",": Compact null hypersurfaces and collapsing Riemannian manifolds. eprint arXiv:","pages","October"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[16] Rendall, Alan.D.: Compact null hypersurfaces and collapsing Riemannian manifolds. eprint arXiv:dg-ga/9510002, pages dg–ga/9510002, October (1995)"}],"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/400532"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1112/blms/15.5.401"],"label":"17"},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[17] Peter Scott: The geometries of $3$-manifolds, ['Bull.London Math.Soc.,15,401-487'], DOI: 10.1112/blms/15.5.401"}]}],"keywords":[{"source":"author","value":"Cauchy horizons"},{"source":"author","value":"Cosmological spacetimes"},{"source":"author","value":"Null generators"},{"source":"author","value":"Symmetries"}],"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","number_of_pages":10,"legacy_creation_date":"2020-08-28","preprint_date":"2020-08-27","author_count":2,"public_notes":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"10 pgs"}],"earliest_date":"2020-08-27","refereed":true,"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"MSNET","value":"4235760"}],"facet_author_name":["2333930_Martín Reiris Ithurralde","2346774_Ignacio Bustamante"],"license":[{"license":"arXiv nonexclusive-distrib 1.0","material":"preprint","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:1813622","updated":"2026-04-01T05:02:03.511540"},"journal_title_variants":["Gen. Rel. Grav.","Gen.Rel.Grav."],"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["gr-qc","math.DG"],"value":"2008.11926"}],"referenced_authors_bais":["V.Moncrief.1","K.Lake.1","E.Minguzzi.1","P.T.Chrusciel.1","I.Racz.1","O.L.Petersen.1","A.D.Rendall.1","J.Isenberg.1"],"inspire_categories":[{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology","source":"arxiv"},{"term":"Math and Math Physics","source":"arxiv"}],"legacy_version":"20210419181255.0","first_author":{"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"GRID","value":"grid.11630.35"},{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/030bbe882"}],"full_name":"Bustamante, Ignacio","last_name":"Bustamante","first_name":"Ignacio","recid":2346774},"control_number":1813622,"dois":[{"source":"Springer","value":"10.1007/s10714-021-02809-z"},{"source":"bibmatch","value":"10.1007/s10714-021-02809-z"}],"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Bustamante:2020mjy","Reiris:2020mdw"],"abstracts":[{"source":"Springer","value":"We establish a complete classification theorem for the topology and for the orbital type of the null generators of compact non-degenerate Cauchy horizons of time orientable smooth vacuum $3+1$-spacetimes. We show that one and only one of the following must hold: (i) all generators are closed, (ii) only two generators are closed and any other densely fills a two-torus, (iii) every generator densely fills a two-torus, or (iv) every generator densely fills the horizon. We then show that, respectively to (i)–(iv), the horizon’s manifold is either: (i’) a Seifert manifold, (ii’) a lens space, (iii’) a two-torus bundle over a circle, or, (iv’) a three-torus. All the four possibilities are known to arise in examples. In the last case, (iv), (iv’), we show in addition that the spacetime is indeed flat Kasner, thus settling a problem posed by Isenberg and Moncrief for ergodic horizons. The results of this article open the door for a full parameterization of the metrics of all vacuum spacetimes with a compact Cauchy horizon. The method of proof permits direct generalizations to higher dimensions.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Springer"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"We establish a complete classification theorem for the topology and for the null generators of compact non-degenerate Cauchy horizons of time orientable smooth vacuum $3+1$-spacetimes. We show that, either: (i) all generators are closed, or (ii) only two generators are closed and any other densely fills a two-torus, or (iii) every generator densely fills a two-torus, or (iv) every generator densely fills the horizon. We then show that, respectively to (i)-(iv), the horizon's manifold is either: (i') a Seifert manifold, or (ii') a lens space, or (iii') a two-torus bundle over a circle, or, (iv') a three-torus. All the four possibilities are known to arise in examples. In the last case, (iv), (iv'), we show in addition that the spacetime is indeed flat Kasner, thus settling a problem posed by Isenberg and Moncrief for ergodic horizons. The results of this article open the door for a full parameterization of the metrics of all vacuum spacetimes with a compact Cauchy horizon. The method of proof permits direct generalizations to higher dimensions.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["gr-qc"],"titles":[{"source":"Springer","title":"A classification theorem for compact Cauchy horizons in vacuum spacetimes"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"A classification theorem for compact Cauchy horizons in vacuum spacetimes"}],"imprints":[{"date":"2021-03-25"}],"curated":false},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1813622?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1813622?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1813622?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1813622?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1813622?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1813622?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1813622"},"id":"1813622"},{"created":"2022-01-12T03:05:02.025570+00:00","updated":"2026-02-09T12:12:00.476773+00:00","metadata":{"documents":[{"filename":"document","fulltext":true,"key":"bb59e05416c9960b2e4edf7b002f0919","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/bb59e05416c9960b2e4edf7b002f0919"}],"authors":[{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Facultad de Matemática, Astronomía, Física y Computación (FaMAF), Universidad Nacional de Córdoba, Ciudad Universitaria, Córdob